From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:03:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 329/342] usb_audio: ignore an alternate without an endpoint

A streaming interface's alternate whose endpoint descriptor is missing
(a configuration read while the device was still settling) was chosen
like any other, and Stream::_ChooseAlternate() then read its endpoint
address through NULL: a kernel page fault at 0x6 when such a device was
offered as new. It is skipped now, like one without its format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Stream.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Stream.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Stream.cpp
index 474c2cbd9f..0f88f2b7f8 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Stream.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Stream.cpp
@@ -66,6 +66,12 @@ Stream::_ChooseAlternate()
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		if (fAlternates[i]->Endpoint() == NULL) {
+			// a configuration read badly (see OnSetConfiguration())
+			TRACE(ERR, "Ignore alternate %d - no endpoint.\n", i);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		if (fAlternates[i]->Format()->fFormatType
 				!= USB_AUDIO_FORMAT_TYPE_I) {
 			TRACE(ERR, "Ignore alternate %d - format type %#02x "
